Z||000000||walsh2001||10-22-2001||09:23 AM||||Allright, everyone say a prayer... My GT is in the shop today getting a new clutch put in ($500, I found a good deal). As long as they have the engine down, is there anything else I should have them look at? <P>I installed my new KYB shocks and struts at the Base Auto Hobby Shop last week... it was an easy job Wade87GT came out, and the job went smoothly! (They make for an awesome ride!)<P>Jason<P>------------------<BR>'87 Fiero GT ... Cherry Red||||reg||3
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||10-22-2001||09:52 AM||||If they have access, it wouldn't hurt to check that pesky cabin side exhaust manifold.<BR>Gary<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||10-22-2001||09:56 AM||||You might want to check the axle seal on that side to see if it was leaking.  Prime time to replace it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000003||Phil||10-22-2001||09:59 AM||||If you pull the exhaust manifolds - would be a great time to port them, 8-10 free hp||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||10-22-2001||09:20 PM||||Maybe the rear main seal,axle seals,motor mounts,heater hoses.<BR>If they drop the motor with the tranny,and not just the tranny,maybe it'd be a good time to put in a new water pump.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierozilla||10-23-2001||02:04 AM||||What kind of clutch are they using? I heard Fieros are notorious for rejecting any clutch that is not either GM or Borg-Warner, but I cant back that up.<BR>Also yes, may want to have them check the forward exhaust manifold while the engine is out.||||reg||1
